= Constitutional Debates: Women's Suffrage

The Cortes turn their attention to the universal suffrage, Article 36 of the constitutional draft. Two female deputies lead the debate in the chamber: Clara Campoamor (PRR) and Victoria Kent (PRRS). Campoamor defends women's vote as an unalienable human right saying that "I'm a citizen before I'm a woman". Kent instead argued that Spanish women, deprived of education and social autonomy, are not yet politically prepared, stating that women's suffrage will lead to a conservative parliament in future elections.

This electoral fear divides the PSOE. Socialist intellectual Margarita Nelken supports Kent's thought as granting the vote before liberating women from church influence will work against the socialists, convincing Indalecio Prieto and the party leadership to oppose Article 36. However, reformists like Julián Besteiro, Luis Jiménez de asúa or Fernando de los Ríos reject this opposition for being paternalistic. 

- @support_campoamor: Whip the party to vote YES alongside Clara Campoamor for democratic principle.
- @support_kent_nelken: Whip the party to vote NO alongside Victoria Kent and the Nelken doctrine.

@support_campoamor
title: Support Clara Campoamor and vote YES for universal women's suffrage
on-arrival: pro_republic += 5; prietistas_dissent += 10; workers_ap += 5; rural_ap += 5; middle_ap += 10; smallholders_ap += 10

We side with democratic principle over electoral calculation, voting solidly in favor of Article 36. Most of the socialist deputies combined with Campoamor's radicals and regionalists vote yes, Acción Republicana and the PRRS vote against alongside many radicals and rightists. The motion passes with 161 votes in favor to 121 against and 188 abstentions.

Indalecio Prieto leaves the chamber muttering that the vote is "a stab in the heart to the <span style="color: #E3000F;">Re</span><span style="color: #D5AC27;">pub</span><span style="color: #8845ba;">lic</span>."

@support_kent_nelken
title: Back Victoria Kent and the Nelken thesis to delay women's vote
on-arrival: prietistas_dissent += 10; workers_ap += 5; rural_ap += 5; middle_ap += 10; smallholders_ap += 10; caballeristas_dissent += 5; workers_psoe -= 7; middle_psoe -= 10

Althought we support the equality between men and women, this would hurt greatly the socialist movement. We must vote against women's suffrage until they've been educated on republican values. 

During the roll call, a major rebellion breaks out: dozens of socialist deputies led by Besteiro, de los Ríos and Asúa break party discipline and vote YES alongside Campoamor!

Article 36 passes anyway! Women gain the right to vote, but the PSOE leadership suffers a humiliating public defeat.